      "body": "## Why\n\nParallel research branches contain overlapping packages, claims, and validation receipts. This PR consolidates their recorded work into one reviewable tree, preserves exact source versions and attribution, and replaces superseded source PRs.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Consolidate **138 topic branch names, 169 archived source snapshots, and 612 claims**. The [branch manifest](https://github.com/1337isnot1337/matrix-mult-bounds/blob/e38eb5c21c3e840cd900bfa85c1a4a6808e530fe/docs/consolidation/2026-10-23/branches.json) records exact heads, PR metadata, and recovery tags.\n- Preserve distinct implementations, tests, certificates, and historical archives. Reconcile shared summaries without dropping scope corrections. The [guide](https://github.com/1337isnot1337/matrix-mult-bounds/blob/e38eb5c21c3e840cd900bfa85c1a4a6808e530fe/docs/consolidation/2026-10-23/PUBLICATION.md) and [resolution manifest](https://github.com/1337isnot1337/matrix-mult-bounds/blob/e38eb5c21c3e840cd900bfa85c1a4a6808e530fe/docs/consolidation/2026-10-23/central_resolution_manifest.json) explain selection and conflict decisions.\n- Integrate the recorded main at `9bcee612`, which independently squash-merged PR217's already captured biform work. Preserve concurrent commits `5d144109` and `434178af` separately from the topic-snapshot count. The former corrects one oblique claim: every first map satisfies the lower bound, and the supplied map attains equality. Original source hashes, review flags, and attribution remain recorded.\n- Add the scoped finite-field interpolation continuation and its bounded test. Preserve the quadratic-kernel investigation as an open question. Retain the full four-group Python 3.10/3.14 matrix, archive replay, and auxiliary Lean build.\n\n## Validation\n\n| Local stage | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Full baseline | 1,916 tests executed: 1,914 passed; two stale dependency-pin checks failed. Both pins were repaired with original metadata retained. |\n| Repair and package follow-up | All 29 checks passed. |\n| Eight-head catch-up | All 33 checks and the standalone quadratic equal-degree verifier passed. |\n| Prior closure metadata | Both checks passed. |\n| Five-head gate at `72f5c524` | All 28 checks passed. |\n| Claim/link checks at `33a0f407` | Both checks passed. |\n| Latest frozen tree at `147db331` | All four checks passed in 2.233 seconds. |\n\nThe published snapshot inventory is **1,951 tests across 437 modules**. Coverage combines revision-specific stages; there has been no uninterrupted local full-suite run on the final tree. The [evidence index](https://github.com/1337isnot1337/matrix-mult-bounds/blob/e38eb5c21c3e840cd900bfa85c1a4a6808e530fe/docs/consolidation/2026-10-23/packaged_evidence_index.json) preserves each receipt and its scope.\n\n**Final-head hosted CI remains required:** all eight Python jobs, archive replay, and Lean. Current-main and review gates also apply before merge.\n\n## Research status and cleanup\n\nClaims retain their evidence and review statuses. Consolidation establishes no exponent improvement or independent mathematical review. Lean covers the auxiliary finite-slope lemma; the complete scalar-profile proof remains outside that formalization.\n\nVerified prior cleanup: **127 source branches deleted and 100 source PRs closed as superseded**. **PRs #217 and #215 actually merged independently** and are recorded separately. PR #215 advanced main to `6e11f7c1` using the exact column-overlap source already contained in this snapshot; its new ancestry is being reconciled before the final merge.\n\nAfter this publication, PRs #213 and #216 were closed as superseded and four exact source refs were deleted. Only the quadratic topic branch remains alongside `main` and the consolidation branch. Retirement requires exact archived, incorporated heads; fresh PR/protection checks; no open head/base dependency; and expected-SHA deletion leases. Original bodies, ready/draft and auto-merge metadata, and temporary publication holds remain preserved. Advanced heads are retained.\n\nFinal verified retirement result: **131 source branches deleted and 102 source PRs closed as superseded during this consolidation phase; all deleted heads have exact recovery tags**.\n\n\n## Remaining current-source update\n\nThe quadratic branch advanced to `c7b7257bac3c000543de66a27b3485a29589156c` after this 169-snapshot capture. Its exact head is archived, and its new claim, proof, tests, source-pin reconciliation, and summary qualifications are being integrated in a focused follow-up. PR #218 and that branch remain open. PR #214 remains draft until this last update is published and retired; final-head required CI and current-main/review gates still apply.\n",
